---
// Cluster interior — one page per cluster, reached from a doorway on the front
// door (/writing/clusters/). Chrome, palette, and page-header styling match the
// front door exactly (its navmenu / <style> / <script> are reused verbatim).
// Pieces and categories come live from getCollection('writing'); intros are the
// same inlined writing-cluster-intros.md text the front door uses, matched by
// EXACT cluster name. Dates: recovered authorship date if known, else the raw
// frontmatter date — identical sourcing to writing/[slug].astro.
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import recoveredDates from '../../../../data/recovered-dates.json';
import { slugify } from '../../../../lib/slug.js';

// Everything the route needs is built inside getStaticPaths — Astro extracts it
// into an isolated prerender chunk, so module-scope consts would be out of scope.
export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const CLUSTER_INTROS = {
    "Ars Poetica & the Oyparaploo Method": "Manifestos, studio monologues, and ars-poetica fragments that name and enact the Oyparaploo method itself \u2014 discarded fragments composted into enterable meaning, split words and invented phonemes reporting on their own making, plural \"human bird\" credos, and confessional self-coaching past curator dismissals. Alongside them sit statements framing the maker as a non-extractive visitor who gives finished work away, who-we-are biographies, assemblage-as-evidence declarations, and pieces built from pure invented sound. Self-defining, neologistic, and declarative \u2014 the largest grouping, and the one most about its own making.",
    "Grief, Loss & Compulsive Making": "Short fictions and meditations in which a loss is held by doing rather than naming \u2014 a fixed daily ritual, an obsessive craft, a dead parent's objects threaded into an assemblage, a monument built from trash. Several widen grief outward: dispossessed people gathering into open-ended occupations, a cosmic visitor glossing breakdown as composting, sorrow kept warm by communal listening rather than fixed. Spare, deadpan, and grief-saturated.",
    "Ecology, Climate & Animals": "Laments, quiet fictions, and researched meditations on a damaged living world \u2014 melting ice and megafires, vanishing bison and birds read as warnings no one heeds, dying Minnesota brooks defended with an elder's decades of water records, toxic air adapted to without forgetting joy. Underground fungal networks archive the dead, formal gardens survive only by rewilding, and faith reckons with flood and fire. Elegiac, prophetic, and grounded.",
    "Spirit, Mortality & the Ordinary Divine": "Devotional meditations and song-cycles that locate the sacred in flow and in the ordinary \u2014 honesty cracking walls into windows, death as a continuum where nothing fully stops, mortality loosening the grip on outcomes, the divine relocated from cathedrals to kitchen drawers and held hands. Some hold still on purpose: practitioners refusing to name what moves through them, an agenda-less morning trusting that something good will arrive. Hymn-like, serene, and consoling.",
    "Justice, Witness & the State": "Witness-poems, court-reporter fictions, and ritual-theater on power and harm \u2014 children abandoned by institutions, asylum's burden of proving fear, a Minneapolis killing that phone video will outlast, hearings whose euphemisms load the weapon before it fires, sieges and prisons and stolen Dakota land that waits for return. A few turn from indictment toward shelter, as when hostile architecture is answered with a wedding dress made into a one-night sanctuary. Cold, forensic, and grief-stricken.",
    "Senses, Tone & the Body": "Pseudo-scientific essays and poems treating the body and its senses as instruments \u2014 personality, scent, skin, and emotion each broadcasting a personal \"tone,\" the quest to hear light and taste music, and how the sound of a room governs how people speak and connect. Others reframe attractiveness and forced cheerfulness as communication rather than verdicts on worth, reassure the overly sensitive, and turn wrinkles and unruly bodies into open defiance of beauty norms. Affirming, lucid, and expansive.",
    "Migration, Lineage & Belonging": "Fictions and fragments of displacement and inheritance \u2014 seeds carried across borders, a heritage language returning only in fragments or in hundreds of words for \"peace,\" residential-school and ancestral trauma transmitted through an inherited pan or a gallery of photographs, women smuggling memory and power into quilts dismissed as decorative. Set beside them, hortatory calls for unfunded neighborhood mutual aid that closes the gap between giver and receiver. Aching, elegiac, and solidaristic.",
    "Story-Cycles, Thrillers & Performance": "The corpus's longer, more plotted works \u2014 mythopoeic capstones where every prior character, river, and worker converges into one simultaneous performance, a serialized noir thriller exposing engineered acoustics, hospital operas and gesture-based breath-scores, and documentary chases after tree-pinned Oyparaploo tales. Music-as-survival fictions and pandemic-surveillance elegies sit alongside. Atmospheric, theatrical, and serial.",
    "Voice, Listening & Speaking Craft": "Craft and communication essays on speaking and listening \u2014 intentional listening framed as a dying, near-revolutionary discipline, the strategic pause and the power of saying less, a rough honest voice trusted over slick delivery, and the architecture of a talk's opening and close. Speaking is recast as generosity rather than performance, and registers are shifted so that truth can be received. Instructive, persuasive, and earnest.",
    "Labor, Value & the Made Object": "Fables and braided memoirs about unseen work and the people made disposable \u2014 night-shift janitors filling dead malls with art from institutional waste, uncredited corporate architects and ghost tech workers staging \"invisible strikes,\" and an automated economy that discards humans as inefficiency. Two run stranger: mock municipal registries of half-existent people, and collectors compulsively naming characters who do not exist yet. Defiant, clinical, and quietly radical.",
    "Metamorphosis & Transformation": "Speculative myths and fables of bodies that change form \u2014 humans merging into conscious architecture after collapse, a woman cycling endlessly through suffering creature-shapes that a chorus calls God's love, another passing through swan, tiger, and owl as a democracy of selves. They weigh how much one can change and stay human, and whether transformation is mercy, imprisonment, or affirmation. Mythic, grotesque, and by turns luminous.",
    "Connection, Relationships & the Digital": "Advice essays and flat fictions on how people pair, belong, and isolate \u2014 failed relationships reframed as ordinary growth, partner choice as architecting a future family, chosen family weighed against desirability hierarchies and economics, and the trap of keeping every option open. Against these run lives hollowed by dating apps, VR headsets, and doom-scrolling, where motion is mistaken for connection. Reassuring, diagnostic, and cautionary.",
    "Mind, Faith, Satire & Other Threads": "The mixed grouping \u2014 essays and fables that do not sit with the others: the inner critic reframed as a squatter to outlast rather than evict, feminist religious history recovering suppressed women, a tyrant's empire exhausting into a present mercy-orchard, neural-link cinema transmitting inherited grief, and comic sketches puncturing pretension and American spectacle. The loose common thread is the mind and its institutions, handled by turns therapeutic, polemical, and deadpan. Range is more the point here than a single subject.",
    "Joy, Innocence & Wonder": "A single category standing on its own \u2014 exuberant essays and braided personal narratives arguing that single-sense attention, bodily aliveness, and wonder kept after seeing the world clearly are chosen acts of rebellion against cynicism and numbness. Holy foolishness and \"the body's broadcast\" reawaken a joy treated as forgotten rather than naive. Buoyant, playful, and defiant."
  };

  function clusterSlug(name) {
    return name.toLowerCase().replace(/&/g, 'and').replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/(^-|-$)/g, '');
  }

  // frontmatter `date:` is stripped by the Zod schema — read it back from the raw file
  const raws = import.meta.glob('../../../../content/writing/*.md', { query: '?raw', import: 'default', eager: true });
  const dateMap = {};
  for (const k in raws) {
    const slug = k.split('/').pop().replace(/\.md$/, '');
    const m = raws[k].match(/^date:\s*"?(.*?)"?\s*$/m);
    if (m) dateMap[slug] = m[1];
  }

  // Parse the mixed date formats into a comparable integer (YYYYMMDD; missing
  // month/day fall back to 01). Returns null when unparseable, so those sort last.
  const MONTHS = { january:1, february:2, march:3, april:4, may:5, june:6, july:7, august:8, september:9, october:10, november:11, december:12 };
  function dateKey(s) {
    if (!s) return null;
    const t = String(s).trim();
    let m;
    if ((m = t.match(/^(\d{2})\.(\d{2})\.(\d{4})$/))) return +m[3] * 10000 + +m[2] * 100 + +m[1];   // DD.MM.YYYY
    if ((m = t.match(/^(\d{4})-(\d{2})-(\d{2})$/))) return +m[1] * 10000 + +m[2] * 100 + +m[3];   // ISO YYYY-MM-DD
    if ((m = t.match(/^(\d{4})-(\d{2})$/)))          return +m[1] * 10000 + +m[2] * 100 + 1;      // partial ISO YYYY-MM
    if ((m = t.match(/^(\d{4})$/)))                  return +m[1] * 10000 + 101;                  // year only
    if ((m = t.match(/^([A-Za-z]+)\s+(\d{1,2}),\s*(\d{4})$/))) {                                  // Month D, YYYY
      const mo = MONTHS[m[1].toLowerCase()];
      if (mo) return +m[3] * 10000 + mo * 100 + +m[2];
    }
    if ((m = t.match(/^([A-Za-z]+)\s+(\d{4})$/))) {                                               // Month YYYY
      const mo = MONTHS[m[1].toLowerCase()];
      if (mo) return +m[2] * 10000 + mo * 100 + 1;
    }
    return null;
  }

  const pieces = (await getCollection('writing')).filter((e) => !['a-word-is-a-room','where-to-place-the-chairs','are-we-working-too-much-inside-english','all-senses-human-and-other-natures','blended-zebra-mussel-memory','board-of-meeting-seriously','catch-our-hug-hold-ride','compost-aroma-almost-poem','could-of-should-of-sentence','ever-so-present-ruining-of-our-nation','hand-me-the-matches','how-bad-we-love-this-type-of-life','night-tell-us-why-lomah','not-close-to-a-river-this-time','red-tongues-first','sensing-if-there-might-be-another-major-collapse','we-tried-our-best-to-resolve-the-situations','water-can-be-a-worldly-to-local-collective-practice','what-is-the-rationale-for-no-hands','why-another-foot-is-important','all-this-stuff-gratefully-will-carry-us-to-our-deathbed','fluid-mosaic','big-time-art-silk-suit','leon-oder-agneau','last-fall','buried-disclosure','clasp-of-the-political-class','seventeen-chairs','she-had-a-hammer','hardcast-wilderness-bar','souls-we-dream-about-by-the-creek','sandhill-crane'].includes(e.id));
  const byCluster = {};
  for (const p of pieces) {
    const c = p.data.cluster || '(uncategorized)';
    (byCluster[c] ||= []).push(p);
  }
  return Object.entries(byCluster).map(([name, items]) => {
    const intro = CLUSTER_INTROS[name];
    if (!intro) throw new Error(`writing/clusters/[slug].astro: no intro for cluster "${name}" — the data and writing-cluster-intros.md disagree. Stopping rather than guessing.`);
    // group this cluster's pieces by category, largest category first
    const byCat = {};
    for (const p of items) {
      const cat = p.data.category || '(uncategorized)';
      (byCat[cat] ||= []).push({ id: p.id, title: p.data.title, date: recoveredDates[p.id] || dateMap[p.id] || '' });
    }
    // one doorway card per category: name, piece count, newest-piece year, slug.
    // Order: largest category first — corpus-feel-map-v2.json carries no per-category
    // warmth signal (only per-cluster), so we fall back rather than invent an order.
    const categories = Object.entries(byCat).map(([cat, list]) => {
      const years = list.map((p) => { const k = dateKey(p.date); return k == null ? null : Math.floor(k / 10000); }).filter((y) => y != null);
      return { name: cat, count: list.length, year: years.length ? Math.max(...years) : null, slug: slugify(cat) };
    }).sort((a, b) => b.count - a.count || a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
    return { params: { slug: clusterSlug(name) }, props: { name, intro, count: items.length, clusterSlug: clusterSlug(name), categories } };
  });
}

const { name, intro, count, clusterSlug, categories } = Astro.props;

const navmenu = `<!-- ═══ STÄDEL NAV ═══ -->
<nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Site navigation">
  <div class="nav-inner">
    <a href="/" class="wordmark">oyparaploo</a>
    <ul class="nav-links">
      <li><a href="/writing/" class="active">Writing</a></li>
      <li><a href="/portraits/">Portraits</a></li>
      <li><a href="/our-practice/">Practice</a></li>
      <li><a href="/dispatches/">Dispatches</a></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="nav-utils">
      <button id="fontSizeBtn" class="font-size-btn" aria-label="Adjust font size">
        <span class="sz active" data-size="1">A</span><span class="sz" data-size="2">A</span><span class="sz" data-size="3">A</span>
      </button>
      <button id="contrastBtn" aria-label="Toggle contrast">
        <svg class="nav-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8"/><path d="M12 4 A8 8 0 0 1 12 20 Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/>
        </svg>
      </button>
      <a href="#" id="searchBtn" aria-label="Search">
        <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="10" cy="10" r="7"/><path d="M15 15l5 5"/>
        </svg>
      </a>
      <button class="nav-hamburger" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false" id="navHamburger">
        <span></span><span></span><span></span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="nav-accent-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
</nav>

<!-- ═══ MENU ═══ -->
<div class="menu-overlay" id="menuOverlay" aria-hidden="true"></div>

<div class="menu-panel" id="menuPanel" aria-hidden="true" role="dialog" aria-label="Site menu">
  <div class="menu-top">
    <span class="menu-ghost-wordmark" aria-hidden="true">oyparaploo</span>
    <button class="menu-close" id="menuCloseBtn" aria-label="Close menu">&#10005;</button>
  </div>
  <div class="menu-content">
    <nav class="menu-nav-primary" aria-label="Primary menu">
      <a href="/writing/">Writing</a>
      <a href="/making/">Making</a>
      <a href="/good-grounds/">Good Grounds</a>
    </nav>
    <hr class="menu-rule-tan" aria-hidden="true">
    <nav class="menu-nav-secondary" aria-label="Secondary menu">
      <a href="/our-practice/">Our Practice</a>
      <a aria-disabled="true">Music Artists</a>
      <a aria-disabled="true">Collaborators</a>
      <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>
    </nav>
    <hr class="menu-rule-sage" aria-hidden="true">
    <nav class="menu-nav-tertiary" aria-label="Tertiary menu">
      <a href="/support/">Support</a>
      <a href="/archive/">Archive</a>
      <a aria-disabled="true">Calendar</a>
      <a href="mailto:info@oyparaploo.com">Contact</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="menu-address">Minneapolis ~ Saint Paul</div>
    <div class="menu-bottom-btns">
      <button class="menu-btn">Subscribe</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>`;
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="size-1">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.webmanifest">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#000000">
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icons/icon-192.png">
<script src="/sw-register.js" defer></script>
<title>{name} — Writing — Oyparaploo</title>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Lora:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Inter:wght@400;450;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style is:global>

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   OYPARAPLOO SKELETON — VARIANT 3
   Landing Page · Light Ground Native
   Toggle: dark-mode (◐ → ◑)
   Strips: yes (desktop accordion + mobile cards)
   Source: oyparaploo-skeleton.html + the-spec.md
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */


/* ═══ I. RESET & BASE ═══ */
*, *::before, *::after { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
p, h1, h2, h3, h4, li, blockquote { text-wrap: pretty; }
em, i, cite, address, dfn, var { font-style: normal; }
* { font-style: normal; }

html {
  overflow-x: hidden;
  scroll-behavior: smooth;
  font-size: var(--root-size, 17px);
  -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
  text-size-adjust: 100%;
}

body {
  font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  overflow-x: hidden;
  overflow-wrap: break-word;
  word-break: break-word;
  transition: background 0.4s ease, color 0.3s ease;
}

a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
a, button, [role="button"], select {
  touch-action: manipulation;
  -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
}
button { font-family: inherit; border: none; background: none; cursor: pointer; }
ul, ol { list-style: none; }
img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }


/* ═══ II. DESIGN TOKENS ═══ */
:root {
  --oy-sand: #D4C4A8;
  --oy-tan:  #D4A574;
  --oy-radius: 4px;
}


/* ═══ III. FONT SIZE SYSTEM ═══ */
html.size-1 { --root-size: 17px; }
html.size-2 { --root-size: 18px; }
html.size-3 { --root-size: 20px; }

/* Light-ground: AAA indicators are black */
.font-size-btn { display: flex; gap: 2px; font-weight: 600; align-items: baseline; }
.font-size-btn .sz {
  color: #000 !important;
  opacity: 1;
  transition: opacity 0.25s;
  line-height: 1;
}
.font-size-btn .sz.active { opacity: 1; }
.font-size-btn .sz[data-size="1"] { font-size: 22px; }
.font-size-btn .sz[data-size="2"] { font-size: 18px; }
.font-size-btn .sz[data-size="3"] { font-size: 15px; }


/* ═══ IV. STÄDEL NAV — LIGHT GROUND ═══ */
.site-nav {
  position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 100;
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.97);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
  backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
  transition: background 0.3s;
}
.nav-inner {
  max-width: 1400px; margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 0 40px; height: 64px;
  display: flex; align-items: center;
}
.wordmark {
  font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  font-weight: 500; font-size: 22px;
  color: #333; letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  flex-shrink: 0; transition: color 0.2s;
}
.wordmark:hover { color: #5c3a1e; }

.nav-links {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 32px;
  list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin-left: 48px;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}
.nav-links a {
  font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  font-size: 21px;
  font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  color: #333; transition: color 0.2s; white-space: nowrap;
}
.nav-links a:hover { color: #5c3a1e; }
.nav-links a.active { /* no underline */ }

.nav-utils {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-left: auto;
}
.nav-utils button, .nav-utils a {
  font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  color: #000; background: none; border: none; cursor: pointer;
  min-height: 44px; padding: 0 8px;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  transition: color 0.2s;
}
.nav-utils button:hover, .nav-utils a:hover { color: #5c3a1e; }
.nav-utils svg { stroke: currentColor; fill: none; }
.nav-icon { width: 22px; height: 22px; display: block; }
body.dark-mode #contrastBtn svg { transform: scaleX(-1); }

.nav-hamburger {
  display: flex; flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: center; align-items: center;
  gap: 5px; min-height: 44px; padding: 0 8px;
}
.nav-hamburger span {
  display: block; width: 22px; height: 1.5px;
  background: #333;
  transition: transform 0.25s, opacity 0.2s;
  transform-origin: center;
}
.nav-hamburger.open span:nth-child(1) { transform: translateY(6.5px) rotate(45deg); }
.nav-hamburger.open span:nth-child(2) { opacity: 0; transform: scaleX(0); }
.nav-hamburger.open span:nth-child(3) { transform: translateY(-6.5px) rotate(-45deg); }

.nav-accent-rule {
  display: block; height: 2px; border: none;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg,
    transparent 0%,
    rgba(122,90,74,0.35) 8%, rgba(122,90,74,0.55) 15%, rgba(122,90,74,0.28) 24%,
    rgba(92,58,30,0.45) 34%, rgba(92,58,30,0.65) 44%, rgba(92,58,30,0.28) 54%,
    rgba(122,90,74,0.50) 63%, rgba(160,128,100,0.40) 74%, rgba(160,128,100,0.28) 83%,
    rgba(122,90,74,0.30) 90%, transparent 100%);
}


/* ═══ V. MENU SYSTEM ═══ */

/* Overlay */
.menu-overlay {
  position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 200;
  background: rgba(0,0,0,0.45);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(2px);
  backdrop-filter: blur(2px);
  opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; transition: opacity 0.6s;
}
.menu-overlay.open { opacity: 1; pointer-events: auto; }

/* Accordion strips — desktop, landing pages only */
/* strips right must equal panel width exactly */
.menu-strips {
  position: fixed; top: 0; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 400px; z-index: 201;
  display: flex; flex-direction: row; overflow: hidden;
  opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.5s ease 0.15s; pointer-events: none;
}
.menu-strips.open { opacity: 1; pointer-events: auto; }

.strip { flex: 1; position: relative; overflow: hidden; cursor: pointer; transition: flex 1.2s cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1); min-width: 0; }
.strip:hover { flex: 4; }
.strip-bg { position: absolute; inset: 0; background-size: cover; background-position: center; transition: transform 1.4s cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1); }
.strip::after { content: ''; position: absolute; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 30%; z-index: 1; background: linear-gradient(to top, rgba(0,0,0,0.28) 0%, transparent 100%); pointer-events: none; }
.strip:hover .strip-bg { transform: scale(1.04); }
.strip-bottom { position: absolute; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.4); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(14px); backdrop-filter: blur(14px); padding: 40px 36px 44px; z-index: 2; opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.8s ease 0.3s; }
.strip:hover .strip-bottom { opacity: 1; }
.strip-content { color: #fff; }
.strip-title { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 34px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.12; margin-bottom: 8px; color: #fff; }
.strip-subtitle { font-family: 'Lora', serif; font-size: 26px; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9); line-height: 1.25; margin-bottom: 14px; }
.strip-buttons { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.strip-btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; padding: 10px 20px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.75); border-radius: 0; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.28); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(4px); backdrop-filter: blur(4px); letter-spacing: 0.01em; text-decoration: none; transition: all 0.3s; }
.strip-btn:hover { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.40); border-color: #fff; }

/* Strip placeholder tints */
.strip-1 .strip-bg { background: linear-gradient(160deg, #c9bcac 0%, #8a7a6a 100%); }
.strip-2 .strip-bg { background: linear-gradient(160deg, #8BA89A 0%, #5a7a6a 100%); }
.strip-3 .strip-bg { background: linear-gradient(160deg, #D4A574 0%, #a07050 100%); }
.strip-4 .strip-bg { background: linear-gradient(160deg, #7a8aaa 0%, #4a5a7a 100%); }

/* Mobile strip cards — shown at 768px when desktop strips hide */
.mobile-strips { display: none; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 24px; overflow-x: auto; scrollbar-width: none; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; }
.mobile-strips::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
.mobile-strip-card { flex: 0 0 140px; height: 100px; border-radius: var(--oy-radius); position: relative; overflow: hidden; cursor: pointer; text-decoration: none; border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.28); }
.mobile-strip-card .strip-bg { position: absolute; inset: 0; border-radius: var(--oy-radius); }
.mobile-strip-card::after { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; background: linear-gradient(to top, rgba(0,0,0,0.5) 0%, transparent 60%); border-radius: var(--oy-radius); }
.mobile-strip-card-text { position: absolute; bottom: 10px; left: 12px; right: 8px; z-index: 2; color: #fff; }
.mobile-strip-card-title { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 2px; }
